{"path":"types/type_info/name","title":"std::type_info::name","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::type_info::</span>name","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/type_info/name","section":"types","kind":"page","summary":"Returns an implementation defined null-terminated character string containing the name of the type.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td><div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> name<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> </td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(noexcept since C++11)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns an implementation defined null-terminated character string containing the name of the type. No guarantees are given; in particular, the returned string can be identical for several types and change between invocations of the same program.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte\">Null-terminated character string</a> containing the name of the type.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The lifetime of the array pointed to by the returned pointer is not specified, but in practice it persists as long as the RTTI data structure for the given type exists, which has application lifetime unless loaded from a dynamic library (that can be unloaded).\n</p><p>Some implementations (such as MSVC, IBM, Oracle) produce a human-readable type name. Others, most notably gcc and clang, return the mangled name, which is specified by the <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://itanium-cxx-abi.github.io/cxx-abi/abi.html#typeid\" data-external=\"1\">Itanium C++ ABI</a>. The mangled name can be converted to human-readable form using implementation-specific API such as <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/libstdc++/manual/ext_demangling.html\" data-external=\"1\"><code>abi::__cxa_demangle</code></a> directly or through <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/release/libs/core/doc/html/core/demangle.html\" data-external=\"1\"><code>boost::core::demangle</code></a>. It can also be piped through the command-line utility <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">c<span class=\"sy2\">++</span>filt <span class=\"sy2\">-</span>t</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;boost/core/demangle.hpp&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdlib&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;typeinfo&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> Base <span class=\"br0\">{</span> <span class=\"kw1\">virtual</span> ~Base<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"kw1\">default</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> Derived <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> Base <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    Base b1<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    Derived d1<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> Base<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> pb <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>b1<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">typeid</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>pb<span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">name</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    pb <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>d1<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">typeid</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>pb<span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">name</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a> real_name <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> boost<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">core</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">demangle</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw1\">typeid</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>pb<span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">name</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">typeid</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>pb<span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">name</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" =&gt; \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> real_name <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"c++filt =&gt; \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/flush\"><span class=\"kw1807\">std::<span class=\"me2\">flush</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a> s <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"kw1\">typeid</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>pb<span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">name</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/program/system\"><span class=\"kw978\">std::<span class=\"me2\">system</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"c++filt -t \"</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> s<span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">data</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>// GCC/Clang:\n4Base\n7Derived\nPK4Base =&gt; Base const*\nc++filt =&gt; Base const*\n&nbsp;\n// MSVC:\nstruct Base\nstruct Derived\nstruct Base const * __ptr64 =&gt; struct Base const * __ptr64</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/type_info/hash_code\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>hash_code</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns a value which is identical for the same types <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"types","title":"Type support (basic types, RTTI)"},{"path":"types/type_info","title":"std::type_info"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::type_info::name","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Returns an implementation defined null-terminated character string containing the name of the type."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Null-terminated character string containing the name of the type."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The lifetime of the array pointed to by the returned pointer is not specified, but in practice it persists as long as the RTTI data structure for the given…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"hash_code","note":"returns a value which is identical for the same types"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":290,"codeBlockCount":2}
